## Video rules (every video)

- 9:16, {{ dims }}, 30 fps, **{{ min }}-{{ max }} s** (`duration`{% if over_minute %}; over 60 s so TikTok's Creator Rewards counts it{% endif %}).
- **No voiceover.** Short second-person story lines, one at a time (`lines`). Each line must be **true and visible
  on screen** at that moment. Every claim and the second it becomes true go in `{{ here }}episodes/<id>/facts.md` with a
  source.
- **Hook in seconds 0-2.** Something new every 2-3 s. The framing changes at least every ~8 s. Escalation speeds
  up, and the last 20 s are the most spectacular. Nothing winds down in the back half.
- **Ending:** {{ ending_text }}
- **Always end with "{{ cta }}"**: the spec's `cta`, e.g. `{"start": {{ cta_start }}, "end": {{ cta_end }}, "text": "{{ cta }}", "sub": "Next: ..."}`{% if loops %}, drawn over the rewind so the loop stays seamless{% endif %}.
{% if hud %}
- **The counter (HUD):** no dark box behind it, and no channel name on it or on the cover. The pipeline does this
  by default: never add `"panel"` or `"show_brand"` to the spec's `hud`, or `"brand"` to its `cover`. It must read
  over any background: QA fails a video whose HUD stays below 4.5:1 contrast for half a second. Don't thin the
  font, drop the outline, or lower the threshold to get a video through.
{% else %}
- No on-screen counter unless a video truly needs one; the story lines carry it.
{% endif %}
- **Look:** {{ style_text }}. The example scenes in `examples/` are the minimum visual standard;
  `docs/QUALITY.md` lists the banned faults.
- **Loudness: {{ lufs }} LUFS integrated.** Both mixers master to it automatically, and QA fails a video louder
  than {{ lufs_fail }} LUFS, with a loudest 3 s above {{ short_fail }} LUFS, or a true peak above {{ tp_fail }} dBTP.
  Never raise it for one video; ask {{ who }} before changing it (`{{ here }}my-studio/studio.toml`).
- **No static, ever.** Beds and long effects come from recordings only; QA fails hiss, loudness blasts and piled-up
  samples (`docs/SOUND.md`).

