## Making a video

1. **Pick the subject.** Never repeat one from `{{ here }}completed videos/production-log.md`. Take the next unused idea in
   the bible's slate, or research a new one (`docs/RESEARCH.md`).
2. **Start the episode:** `{{ py }} -m studio{{ pflag }} new-episode <slug>` makes `{{ here }}episodes/epNN_<slug>/` with an
   `episode.json` and a `facts.md` to fill in.
3. **Script and facts:** `title`, `lines`, `hud`, `cta`, `hashtags`, the sound cue sheet. Check every number;
   write it with its source and the second it becomes true in `facts.md`. No line appears before its fact is true.
4. **Build the scene:** `{{ py }} pipeline{{ sep }}make_episode.py {{ here_cmd }}episodes{{ sep }}<id> --steps build,stills --stills {{ stills }}`
   and **look at every still** in `build/stills/`. Fix and repeat until each one clears `docs/QUALITY.md`. New
   scenes go in new modules (`pipeline/blender/worlds/<name>.py`, `effects/<name>.py`); never change a module
   another episode uses in a way that changes that episode.
5. **Check the text** without a full render: `{{ py }} pipeline{{ sep }}post{{ sep }}compose.py {{ here_cmd }}episodes{{ sep }}<id> --preview {{ preview }}`.
6. **Render:** `--steps render` (20-40 min on a good GPU; run it in the background). It resumes and **skips frames
   that already exist**, so delete `build/frames` after changing the scene.{% if codex %} If your shell stops a long
   command, run it again: it carries on where it stopped.{% endif %}

7. **Post-production:** `--steps post` (sound, video, cover, captions, then QA -> `build/qa/report.md`). It stops on
   any FAIL. A WARN in the sound checks is a reason to fix the mix, not to ship.
8. **Your review:** look at every `build/qa/sheet_*.jpg`, the cover, and full-resolution frames from the final mp4
   at every line and big moment; read both loudness lines in the report; re-check `facts.md`. Write
   `build/qa/review.md` (picture, sound, facts) ending with `APPROVED` or `REJECTED: why`. If you're not sure it's
   right, it isn't done.
9. **Ship:** `--steps ship` copies the video to `{{ here }}completed videos/<id> - <title>/` (only if QA passed on this exact
   file and your review says APPROVED), deletes the render frames, and **checks that ReelForge's Publish tab lists it**
   with the right caption and hashtags. A video is done only when that check says READY.
10. **Log it:** add a row to `{{ here }}completed videos/production-log.md`.
11. **Tell {{ who }}** it's ready in ReelForge -> **Publish**: the title, the length, anything to know.

## Delivering to ReelForge's Publish tab

ReelForge's Publish tab (`reelforge{{ pflag }} publish`) lists every `{{ here }}episodes/<id>/final/<id>.mp4`, newest first, with the post pre-filled from
`episode.json`'s `title` and the hashtag line of `final/caption.txt`. {{ Who }} uploads from there by hand: each
platform's button opens its upload page and copies exactly the text that site needs.
- Keep that layout: `{{ here }}episodes/<id>/episode.json`, `final/<id>.mp4`, `final/caption.txt`, `final/cover.jpg`.
- `{{ py }} -m studio publish-check {{ here_cmd }}episodes{{ sep }}<id>` runs the same check as `ship` at any time and prints
  each platform's post.
- Never upload or post yourself, and never open the platforms' upload pages.

