## Gotchas

- Blender's `keyframe_insert()` ignores the default interpolation: call `rf.set_interpolation(...)`.
- Delete `build/frames` after changing the world or effect, or the render keeps the old frames.
- Run anything that reads downloaded files (e.g. `assets/sfx/`) with `python -I`. Every new sound needs a licence
  entry in `assets/sfx/manifest.json`; Mixkit and Kenney (CC0) are the approved free sources.
- `{{ here }}episodes/` grows by about 0.6 GB per video until `ship` cleans the frames. Keep 10 GB free before a render.
{% if win %}
- Paths can contain spaces or apostrophes: quote them with double quotes, never single quotes.
{% endif %}
